---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const censusAlt =
  "DESI spectroscopic census of dwarf galaxies, showing the distribution of spectroscopically confirmed dwarf galaxies and a smaller comparison sample of pre-DESI dwarfs.";
const censusCaption =
  "The DESI dwarf-galaxy census. Each black point represents a spectroscopically confirmed dwarf galaxy.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sample"
  description="MISTY sample selection from the DESI dwarf-galaxy census."
>
  <article class="sample-page">
    <div class="sample-page__prose">
      <p>
        MISTY selects its targets from the DESI dwarf-galaxy census. In its
        first data release, DESI identified spectroscopically approximately
        500,000 dwarf galaxies to z&nbsp;≤&nbsp;0.2. This number is expected to
        grow to approximately 1,000,000 in the next data release.
      </p>
      <p>
        At the distances targeted by MISTY, DESI is complete for non-quiescent
        systems down to stellar masses of approximately 10<sup>6</sup>&nbsp;M<sub>☉</sub>,
        above μ<sub>V</sub>&nbsp;≈&nbsp;25&nbsp;mag&nbsp;arcsec<sup>−2</sup> and
        subject to emission-line detection limits. We use the dwarf-galaxy{" "}
        <a
          href="https://virajvman.github.io/desidwarfs_webapp/index.html"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">catalog</a>{" "}
        (Manwadkar et al., submitted), which provides photometry, emission-line
        flux measurements, star-formation rates, stellar masses, and additional
        derived properties.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="sample-page__selection-block">
      <figure class="sample-page__figure sample-figure-one--desktop">
        <img
          src="/images/sample/desi-dwarf-census.png"
          alt={censusAlt}
          width="1535"
          height="1240"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>{censusCaption}</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="sample-page__prose sample-page__selection-text">
        <p>
          The DESI dwarf-galaxy population shows substantial diversity in
          star-formation rate and metallicity at fixed stellar mass. MISTY
          selects galaxies within 30&nbsp;Mpc and with stellar masses of
          10<sup>6</sup>–10<sup>8.5</sup>&nbsp;M<sub>☉</sub>. To construct a
          representative population of dwarf galaxies, we sample uniformly in
          the specific-star-formation-rate–metallicity plane. Metallicities are
          estimated from DESI integrated spectra within the
          1.5&nbsp;arcsec-diameter fiber aperture, using the direct
          temperature-sensitive method where possible and the S-cal strong-line
          calibration otherwise.
        </p>

        <figure class="sample-page__figure sample-figure-one--mobile">
          <img
            src="/images/sample/desi-dwarf-census.png"
            alt={censusAlt}
            width="1535"
            height="1240"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>{censusCaption}</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          MISTY also samples the full range of large-scale environments, from
          isolated dwarfs through galaxies in overdense regions to satellites
          and interacting systems. The science goals require the detection of
          weak auroral lines in individual spaxels of the optical IFU data
          cubes. This requirement imposes an emission-line flux threshold
          compatible with observations from Magellan and Keck, while telescope
          location also determines which targets are observable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="sample-page__figure sample-page__figure--selection sample-figure-two">
      <picture>
        <source
          media="(max-width: 639px)"
          srcset="/images/sample/misty-sample-selection-mobile.png"
        />
        <img
          src="/images/sample/misty-sample-selection.png"
          alt="Comparison of the DESI dwarf-galaxy population and MISTY targets in star-formation-rate versus stellar-mass and metallicity versus stellar-mass space."
          width="3600"
          height="1200"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
      <figcaption>
        MISTY in the DESI dwarf-galaxy population. The MISTY targets sample the
        distributions of star-formation activity and gas-phase metallicity at
        fixed stellar mass within the nearby DESI dwarf population.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sample-page {
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .sample-page__prose {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .sample-page__prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1.15em;
  }

  .sample-page__prose p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .sample-page__prose a {
    color: var(--navy);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }

  .sample-page__prose a:hover {
    color: var(--navy-dark);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  .sample-page__selection-block {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .sample-page__figure img,
  .sample-page__figure picture {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .sample-page__figure img {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--surface-strong);
  }

  .sample-page__figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  /* Desktop/tablet: right-floated half-width Figure 1 */
  .sample-figure-one--desktop {
    display: block;
    float: right;
    width: 48%;
    margin: 0 0 16px 32px;
  }

  .sample-figure-one--desktop img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* Mobile instance hidden above the mobile breakpoint */
  .sample-figure-one--mobile {
    display: none;
  }

  .sample-figure-two {
    clear: both;
  }

  .sample-page__figure--selection {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    clear: both;
    float: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .sample-figure-one--desktop {
      display: none;
    }

    .sample-figure-one--mobile {
      display: block;
      float: none;
      width: 100%;
      margin: 24px 0 28px;
    }

    .sample-figure-one--mobile img {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 701px) {
    .sample-page {
      padding-top: 1.65rem;
    }

    .sample-page__prose {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .sample-page__selection-block {
      margin-top: 1.75rem;
    }

    .sample-page__figure figcaption {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }

    .sample-page__figure--selection {
      margin-top: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
